  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190698/assets/78d588198d35e69ca7ae2b199dd52d2c07e5c9d3268214821b737deffe5cb03d.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $∠BOE?$\n\n$m∠BOE=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190698/assets/d3ba77dd51c7d26685246304088d484144f5dcda57c424656ae305cc2ffa78ae.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, we have that $∠COB$ and $∠BOE$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠COB+m∠BOE={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠BOE$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOE & ={180}^{∘}-m∠COB \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{47}^{∘} \\\\  & ={133}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
